+/* The ACCOUNT pads (patch 0012). Kernel memory accounting
+ * (__GFP_ACCOUNT) is not implemented at the doors: no charge is
+ * made, and no call into the core is made for the term on either
+ * side (ruled 2026-11-24). What stands at each door where stock
+ * would spend the term is one of these statements and nothing
+ * else: a breakpoint seat. The alloc seat is reached only by a
+ * request carrying the flag, so a debugger stopped there is
+ * looking at kernel code that asked for accounted memory
+ * through a door; the caller is then to be deduced and ruled
+ * on. The free call carries no flag, so the free seat stands
+ * where stock's uncharge would accompany a door free and is
+ * reached by every door free: the pair seat, not a detector.
+ * The variables are written and never read; volatile keeps the
+ * statements in the build. */
+static volatile int iscandar_account_alloc_pad;
+static volatile int iscandar_account_free_pad;
+
 /*
  * Inlined fastpath so that allocation functions (kmalloc, kmem_cache_alloc)
  * have the fastpath folded into their functions. So no function call
